Installing GAOL v5
==================

GAOL v5 is built with CMake (the build to use), autotools or meson. The
sources of CORE-MATH, which bounds every elementary function of GAOL, are
in 3rd/math-core and are compiled into libgaol itself: there is no
mathematical library to install beforehand, nor to link along with GAOL.

With CMake (3.14 or later):

    cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=<prefix> -DWITH_TESTS=ON
    cmake --build build --config Release
    cmake --build build --target test
    cmake --install build --config Release

With autotools:

    ./configure --prefix=<prefix> --with-tests
    make
    make test
    make install

With meson:

    meson setup build --prefix=<prefix> -Dwith-tests=true
    meson compile -C build
    meson test -C build
    meson install -C build

make test runs the unit tests of tests/, which need nothing else, and make
check the unit tests and the examples of examples/, built with
-DWITH_EXAMPLES=ON, --with-examples or -Dwith-examples=true (ninja check with
meson).

doc/building.md gives the options of each build, and doc/using.md the flags
of interval arithmetic the code including GAOL's headers is compiled with.
